This will be where we keep the full plan for the creation fo the whole directory and pipeline. Everything. 
We keep logs abotu what changes and what we have done. WHat needs to be done etc. 
We should probably set up clear git/github.


What you need in 3 days is two things in parallel:

Composer + Stage C view stays the spine (already proven).

Orchestra stages A/B/D are ported as “workers” and then registered into Stage C and summarised by Composer.

Key principle: Stage code is allowed to be messy internally. The only requirement is it speaks the interface:

A produces a run package (prmtop/inpcrd + metadata)

B consumes a run package and produces raw evidence (prod.nc/out + metadata)

C indexes + exposes evidence via views/runs/...

D consumes only from C view and produces tables/plots + metrics back into Composer state

So: we port the old code, but we wrap it, not rewrite it.

The missing piece: a minimal contract between stages

You will drown unless you standardise exactly one “thing” that moves between A→B→C→D:

run_manifest.json (one per replicate)

Lives alongside the system files / run folder. Minimum fields:

{
  "project": "PET_SCREENING",
  "ligand_norm": "diuron",
  "charge": -50,
  "replica": "rep1",
  "smiles": "...",
  "builder": {"git_commit": "...", "timestamp": "..."},
  "simulator": {"engine": "amber", "settings_id": "local_tiny_v1"},
  "paths": {
    "build_dir": "...",
    "run_dir": "...",
    "archive_dir": "..."
  }
}


Composer doesn’t need to understand AMBER. It needs to understand runs
